    "closedAt": "2025-08-09T16:42:21Z",
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                "login": "echasnovski",
                "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Unfortunately, I don't think there is anything 'mini.sessions' specific that can be done here. It explicitly uses built-in sessions and this is what should be used to adjust here. If 'sessionoptions' doesn't work, then it might be an issue with 'nvim-ufo'.\r\n\r\nFor what it is worth, with `foldmethod=indent` fold state is saved between sessions (if fold was closed/open when writing session, it appears the same after reading session next time).\r\n\r\nIf there is some function/hook that 'nvim-ufo' requires to be executed in such cases, you can use it by defining [`config.hooks.post.read` and or `config.hooks.pre.write`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4035ef97407a6661ae9ff913ff980e271a658502/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L100-L103).",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Unfortunately, I don't think there is anything 'mini.sessions' specific that can be done here. It explicitly uses built-in sessions and this is what should be used to adjust here. If 'sessionoptions' doesn't work, then it might be an issue with 'nvim-ufo'.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For what it is worth, with <code class=\"notranslate\">foldmethod=indent</code> fold state is saved between sessions (if fold was closed/open when writing session, it appears the same after reading session next time).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">If there is some function/hook that 'nvim-ufo' requires to be executed in such cases, you can use it by defining <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4035ef97407a6661ae9ff913ff980e271a658502/doc/mini-sessions.txt#L100-L103\"><code class=\"notranslate\">config.hooks.post.read</code> and or <code class=\"notranslate\">config.hooks.pre.write</code></a>.</p>",
            "bodyText": "Unfortunately, I don't think there is anything 'mini.sessions' specific that can be done here. It explicitly uses built-in sessions and this is what should be used to adjust here. If 'sessionoptions' doesn't work, then it might be an issue with 'nvim-ufo'.\nFor what it is worth, with foldmethod=indent fold state is saved between sessions (if fold was closed/open when writing session, it appears the same after reading session next time).\nIf there is some function/hook that 'nvim-ufo' requires to be executed in such cases, you can use it by defining config.hooks.post.read and or config.hooks.pre.write.",
